    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just romanticizing it. \"complexity and wonder\" doesn't pay the bills or give me a reason to wake up. in any other system, if a part is no longer functional or needed, it's decommissioned. it's just efficient. why should humans be the only exception to the rules of efficiency? it feels like I'm just occupying space that could be used for something that actually matters now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
